#edb/ref 17592186679986} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679988} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679998} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186680002} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186680008} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186680034} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186680041} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186680049} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186680058} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682785} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682792} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682793} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682795} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682796} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682798} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682804} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682816} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682834} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682835} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682841} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682842} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682849} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682856} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682872} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682882}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Indefinite Integrals Using Substitution with Inverse Tangent"} :step/id #uuid "a6a53452-9624-525f-9b54-d025309e71da" :step/math-academy-id 641168 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065124}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065079 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064220 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064092 :question/id #uuid "cb771ff3-b5a9-5900-913f-df23957760b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-472" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle{\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt 2} \\dfrac{1}{2+x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+{x}^{2}/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that this integral now resembles the basic integral for the inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int\\dfrac{1}{1+u^2}\\,\\textrm d u = \\arctan{u} + C.\n$$\n\nWe make the substitution $u=\\dfrac{x}{\\sqrt 2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\sqrt 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048332}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186680285} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064544} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064545} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250184} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250185} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250186} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250187} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287944} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287945} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287946} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319103} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319105} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320815} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320915} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320917} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320918} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320919} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320920} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332736} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332737} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368428} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377538} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428007} {:db/